being Raise a concern or appeal Our Research Main menu Our Research Our focus Our Research Our focus Good lives Exceptional care Strong communities Institutes and initiatives Our Research Institutes and initiatives Institute for Ethics & Society Institute for Health Research Nulungu Research Institute Centre for the History of Philosophy Churack Chair of Chronic Pain Education and Research Global Catholic Studies Global Centre for Catholic Leaders Centre for Technology and Human Futures Integrity and ethics Our Research Integrity and ethics Research integrity Human Research Ethics Research Data Management Engage Main menu Engage Visit us Engage Visit us Sydney Open Day Alumni Engage Alumni Alumni news Alumni perks Alumni volunteering Honorary doctorates Stay connected Donations Engage Donations Greatest Need Student Grants Opportunity and Merit Scholarships Research Fund Gifts in Wills Capital Gifts School of Medicine Prizes Our donors Contact us Industry and business partnerships Career advisors and teachers Venue hire Events News About us Main menu About us Introducing UNDA Our Strategy About us Our Strategy Antisemitism Student Equity and Diversity Strategy Vision and objects About us Vision and objects Our traditions Governance and leadership About us Governance and leadership Our leadership Structure Compliance Act, statutes and regulations Policies, procedures and guidelines Annual Performance Our national faculties and schools About us Our national faculties and schools School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Health Sciences School of Law and Business School of Medicine School of Nursing & Midwifery School of Philosophy & Theology Pathways Our campuses and facilities About us Our campuses and facilities Broome Fremantle Sydney Our community impact Jobs at UNDA About us Jobs at UNDA Employment opportunities Staff benefits Contact us Apply Now Make an enquiry Library Student portal Staff Contact us Join the conversation, connect today. Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Twitter YouTube Home Students Services, resources and tools Career planning and resources Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram Support ND Support Hubs Access and inclusion Study support IT support Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander support HDR student support International student support Regional and rural student support Career planning and resources Emergency contacts Health, safety and wellbeing Raise a concern or appeal Career planning and resources The Careers and Employability team provides valuable career support for students from Year One through to graduation and up to 18 months after graduation. The team also conducts general and School-based workshops, as well as providing a range of career management resources. Support is available in the following areas: Career and course planning Job applications - résumés, cover letters and selection criteria statements Interview skills and techniques Networking and job search techniques Future of work Students and Alumni can access resources, events and make appointments via CareerHub , where guidance and support are available for students who are seeking employment. This kind of personal interaction can lead to more successful career planning, job hunting, confidence building and motivation. CareerHub Current students and recent graduates can go the CareerHub for the following: Access the job board for casual, graduate, internship and vacation opportunities. View career and job resources to help you develop the skills to manage your career, course choices, and job search successfully. Book to attend career and employment events and workshops. Make an appointment to see a Career Officer. Career pathways It is ok to be unsure about your career and course choices. After all it is common for people to change careers 4-5 times in their life in Australia. We can help you eliminate any doubts in your mind about which pathways may suit you and build confidence in navigating a changing workforce. Make a career appointment via CareerHub using your University of Notre Dame login. Before booking an appointment, the following websites may be of use in building self-awareness and gathering employment information: My Career Match : As Notre Dame subscribes to this resource, simply email the Careers Officer for an access code and enter this when you’ve completed your profile. It’s easy to do and surprisingly accurate with a detailed report. 16 Personalities : Is a useful personality test to build a language to describe who you are and why you do the things the way you do. Barrett Personal Values Assessment : Your values reflect what is important to you, your motivations, and your beliefs. This is often forgotten when choosing careers. Skillsroad : A slick, detailed website with a number of quizzes and self-assessment tools more suited to the school leaver. Graduate Careers Australia : Check out their Career planning and resources section. My Future : National career information site. Has partnership with Notre Dame. Create your own profile and explore. Register using your Notre Dame email to access extra information and resources on this Government funded website. Job Outlook : Government funded, comprehensive career information and exploration site. Take the Career Quiz. Don’t forget to consult your School and Discipline coordinators when making such decisions. Career resources Be sure to leave no stone unturned when seeking information. Begin by exploring online resources, the University library and the Career Service to aid you in your career choices. There is a range of literature accessible to Notre Dame Students on topics such as those below on CareerHub and printed material. Simply contact the Career Service for more information. Graduate salaries International students Interviews Labour market information Networking Postgraduate studies Professional associations Psychometric tests Résumés and cover letters Selection criteria Skills auditing Volunteering Working around the globe Information for employers The University of Notre Dame Australia is keen to develop new relationships and maintain current relationships with employers offering opportunities for current students and alumni. This can be through graduate programs or general employment including casual, permanent or vocational positions. We offer the following promotional options: CareerHub : Advertise casual, part-time, internships, graduate and full-time positions. Direct student contact: Target a specific group by direct mail or email. Employer events: Promote your organisation on campus so students know what you can offer. Liaison with faculties and schools for employers wishing to host work placement students or participate in guest lectures and case studies in-class. Contact us Need help? For more information or to get in touch, contact our Careers & Employability Team: Email: career.service@nd.edu.au Fremantle: +61 8 9433 0582 Sydney: +61 2 8204 4434 Locations Online Fremantle Broome Sydney Clinical Schools Quicklinks Donations Alumni Library Faculties and schools Apply direct Emergency Contact us Visit us Uni store Jobs at UNDA Feedback News Events Sydney © 2026 The University of Notre Dame Australia CRICOS Provider Code: 01032F : TEQSA PRV12170 : RTO Code 0064 Privacy Terms of Use"
    },
