ome Fremantle Sydney Our community impact Jobs at UNDA Employment opportunities Staff benefits Contact us Make an enquiry Submit Apply now Study with us Main menu Study with us Explore our programs Study with us Explore our programs Undergraduate Postgraduate Graduate research Vocational Education and Training (VET) Microcredential Online programs Guides Why UNDA? Study with us Why UNDA? Meet our students Our Core Curriculum Applications and admissions Study with us Applications and admissions How to apply Admission requirements Admission pathways Recognition of prior learning Fees, costs and scholarships Study with us Fees, costs and scholarships Tuition fees Other costs Financial assistance Scholarships International students Study with us International students Full degree students Semester abroad at UNDA Moving to Australia Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students Study with us Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students Recognised events Cultural protocols Students Main menu Students Your enrolment Students Your enrolment Calendars and timetables Student Centre Enrolling in courses Enrolment changes Student forms Student policies Student ID and concession cards Exams, results and graduation Fees and payments Glossary of terms Getting started Students Getting started Orientation week Student life Students Student life Accommodation Student Associations Student clubs and societies Sports and recreation Volunteering and mentoring Chaplaincy Opportunities and experiences Students Opportunities and experiences Job opportunities and career events Global experiences Study abroad and exchange programs Short-term travel and study tours Study retreats In Altum Support Students Support ND Support Hubs Access and inclusion Study support IT support Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander support HDR student support International student support Regional and rural student support Career planning and resources Emergency contacts Health, safety and wellbeing Raise a concern or appeal Our Research Main menu Our Research Our focus Our Research Our focus Good lives Exceptional care Strong communities Institutes and initiatives Our Research Institutes and initiatives Institute for Ethics & Society Institute for Health Research Nulungu Research Institute Centre for the History of Philosophy Churack Chair of Chronic Pain Education and Research Global Catholic Studies Global Centre for Catholic Leaders Centre for Technology and Human Futures Integrity and ethics Our Research Integrity and ethics Research integrity Human Research Ethics Research Data Management Engage Main menu Engage Visit us Engage Visit us Sydney Open Day Alumni Engage Alumni Alumni news Alumni perks Alumni volunteering Honorary doctorates Stay connected Donations Engage Donations Greatest Need Student Grants Opportunity and Merit Scholarships Research Fund Gifts in Wills Capital Gifts School of Medicine Prizes Our donors Contact us Industry and business partnerships Career advisors and teachers Venue hire Events News About us Main menu About us Introducing UNDA Our Strategy About us Our Strategy Antisemitism Student Equity and Diversity Strategy Vision and objects About us Vision and objects Our traditions Governance and leadership About us Governance and leadership Our leadership Structure Compliance Act, statutes and regulations Policies, procedures and guidelines Annual Performance Our national faculties and schools About us Our national faculties and schools School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Health Sciences School of Law and Business School of Medicine School of Nursing & Midwifery School of Philosophy & Theology Pathways Our campuses and facilities About us Our campuses and facilities Broome Fremantle Sydney Our community impact Jobs at UNDA About us Jobs at UNDA Employment opportunities Staff benefits Contact us Apply Now Make an enquiry Library Student portal Staff Contact us Join the conversation, connect today. Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Twitter YouTube Home About us Jobs at UNDA Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram Jobs at UNDA An exceptional educational experience requires exceptional people The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to recruit outstanding people who understand and respect Our Objects and have the skill, experience, qualifications, drive and persistence to pursue them. By joining Notre Dame, you will be welcomed into a community committed to service excellence, building knowledge, supporting creativity, and caring for each other and our students. We recognise that every employee is unique and will bring different skills and talents. This is why we are dedicated to supporting our employees to flourish and achieve their potential through various career development and training opportunities. Notre Dame values service excellence and employee growth. Employment opportunities A range of career options, take the next step toward professional success. View opportunity How to apply Learn how to prepare your application and how to apply to Notre Dame. Apply now Staff benefits Discover how we invest in your wellbeing and professional growth. Learn more Why Notre Dame? We provide a liberal arts education in the Catholic intellectual tradition and quality university teaching. As a young and innovative university, we offer our students the theoretical knowledge and professional experiences that prepare them for a rich, fulfilling and reflective life, not just a career path. Student demand for our courses and our learning environment continues to grow. We believe this is in response to the significant satisfaction levels our students and graduates report of their experience at Notre Dame. Notre Dame offers an exceptional educational experience for its 12,000+ students coast to coast. We want our students to grow intellectually and spiritually in all aspects of their lives. Students and employers have recognised our unique approach to university education as among the very best in Australia, as reflected in the Good Universities Guide 2026 results. Our 800+ dedicated employees across our three Campuses in Fremantle, Broome and Sydney and our seven Clinical Schools in NSW and Victoria are integral to our success. About us The story of our university is a remarkable one. It’s a story that begins with a vision to establish Australia’s first university with the Catholic intellectual tradition at its core. Introducing UNDA Discover our journey, Catholic values, bold research and approach that empowers students with lifelong skills. Learn more Vision and objects Our mission and objectives are at the heart of everything we do. We have adopted principles to guide us in achieving them. Learn more Campus and facilities Explore our campuses and clinical schools. Discover our facilities and services that support academic success and wellbeing. Learn more Our faculties and schools We have three national faculties and eight schools in WA and NSW known for their excellent teaching, training, and research. Learn more Working for a Catholic university Since its foundation, the University has sought to create an environment where staff and students feel part of a community, welcoming people from all backgrounds regardless of their faith. As a Catholic university, Notre Dame is committed to the pastoral care of staff and students. Our staff are encouraged to participate in religious, academic and social events hosted throughout the year, creating a strong Christian intellectual life on our three campuses. There are also opportunities to engage with members of the broader community through initiatives such as public lectures, debates and presentations hosted by the University. Notre Dame fosters community, inclusivity, and Christian intellectual engagement. Our 2026 Strategy We invite you to explore our Strategic Plan, we outline our vision to enhance our university and build for the future. Join us as we build a stronger and brighter future together. UNDA Staff Enterprise Agreement The university is committed to negotiating with staff and the union in good faith, being open and transparent in our dealings, and looking for sensible solutions. Employee Code of Conduct and Ethical Behaviour The University of Notre Dame expects all parties to conduct themselves with professional standards and behavior when interacting with other members of the community. Policies and Procedures The Policy Portal contains all university approved policies, procedures and guidelines. You will also find information on how to develop and review university policy documents. Locations Online Fremantle Broome Sydney Clinical Schools Quicklinks Donations Alumni Library Faculties and schools Apply direct Emergency Contact us Visit us Uni store Jobs at UNDA Feedback News Events Sydney © 2026 The University of Notre Dame Australia CRICOS Provider Code: 01032F : TEQSA PRV12170 : RTO Code 0064 Privacy Terms of Use"
    },
