roome Fremantle Sydney Our community impact Jobs at UNDA Employment opportunities Staff benefits Contact us Make an enquiry Submit Apply now Study with us Main menu Study with us Explore our programs Study with us Explore our programs Undergraduate Postgraduate Graduate research Vocational Education and Training (VET) Microcredential Online programs Guides Why UNDA? Study with us Why UNDA? Meet our students Our Core Curriculum Applications and admissions Study with us Applications and admissions How to apply Admission requirements Admission pathways Recognition of prior learning Fees, costs and scholarships Study with us Fees, costs and scholarships Tuition fees Other costs Financial assistance Scholarships International students Study with us International students Full degree students Semester abroad at UNDA Moving to Australia Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students Study with us Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students Recognised events Cultural protocols Students Main menu Students Your enrolment Students Your enrolment Calendars and timetables Student Centre Enrolling in courses Enrolment changes Student forms Student policies Student ID and concession cards Exams, results and graduation Fees and payments Glossary of terms Getting started Students Getting started Orientation week Student life Students Student life Accommodation Student Associations Student clubs and societies Sports and recreation Volunteering and mentoring Chaplaincy Opportunities and experiences Students Opportunities and experiences Job opportunities and career events Global experiences Study abroad and exchange programs Short-term travel and study tours Study retreats In Altum Support Students Support ND Support Hubs Access and inclusion Study support IT support Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander support HDR student support International student support Regional and rural student support Career planning and resources Emergency contacts Health, safety and wellbeing Raise a concern or appeal Our Research Main menu Our Research Our focus Our Research Our focus Good lives Exceptional care Strong communities Institutes and initiatives Our Research Institutes and initiatives Institute for Ethics & Society Institute for Health Research Nulungu Research Institute Centre for the History of Philosophy Churack Chair of Chronic Pain Education and Research Global Catholic Studies Global Centre for Catholic Leaders Centre for Technology and Human Futures Integrity and ethics Our Research Integrity and ethics Research integrity Human Research Ethics Research Data Management Engage Main menu Engage Visit us Engage Visit us Sydney Open Day Alumni Engage Alumni Alumni news Alumni perks Alumni volunteering Honorary doctorates Stay connected Donations Engage Donations Greatest Need Student Grants Opportunity and Merit Scholarships Research Fund Gifts in Wills Capital Gifts School of Medicine Prizes Our donors Contact us Industry and business partnerships Career advisors and teachers Venue hire Events News About us Main menu About us Introducing UNDA Our Strategy About us Our Strategy Antisemitism Student Equity and Diversity Strategy Vision and objects About us Vision and objects Our traditions Governance and leadership About us Governance and leadership Our leadership Structure Compliance Act, statutes and regulations Policies, procedures and guidelines Annual Performance Our national faculties and schools About us Our national faculties and schools School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Health Sciences School of Law and Business School of Medicine School of Nursing & Midwifery School of Philosophy & Theology Pathways Our campuses and facilities About us Our campuses and facilities Broome Fremantle Sydney Our community impact Jobs at UNDA About us Jobs at UNDA Employment opportunities Staff benefits Contact us Apply Now Make an enquiry Library Student portal Staff Contact us Join the conversation, connect today. Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Twitter YouTube Home About us Jobs at UNDA Staff benefits Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram Jobs at UNDA Employment opportunities Staff benefits Staff benefits Remuneration & entitlements Generous parental leave Eligible staff can access up to 26 weeks paid parental leave for primary carers and 2 weeks paid leave for non-primary caregivers. Benefits for staff working at Broome Staff working at the Broome Campus receive remote location benefits, two weeks additional leave and $1,000 location allowance each year. Generous superannuation Continuing and fixed-term staff members receive 13.5% employer superannuation contributions and access on-site UniSuper superannuation advice, seminars and support. Career Development Fund General Staff can apply for financial support to undertake career development activities to develop their professional skills and knowledge in their current position and to enhance their career. Professional development leave Staff can access up to 5 days leave to undertake approved professional development activities. LinkedIn Learning Staff can develop their skills through LinkedIn Learning ’s online educational platform of over 15,000 online courses to develop business, technology-related, and creative skills through expert-led course videos. Discover, complete, and track courses related to your role and build your professional skills to in your role and career aspirations. Study Support Study Support is available to employees employed on a full-time or part-time 0.5 FTE or greater basis and includes: Study Leave of up to 4 hours per week to attend and travel to classes and exams, complete assessments or private study; and Financial Assistance for Study to assist with the payment of fees (via reimbursement) for up to 2 courses per year upon successful completion of an approved course at The University of Notre Dame Australia. Employee family study discount at Notre Dame The University offers a dependent child of an eligible employee 25% discount on tuition fees for full fee paying first degrees and diplomas offered at The University of Notre Dame Australia. For more information check out the Policy: Employee Family Study Discount and complete the Employee Family Study Discount form to apply. Generous long service leave While Notre Dame doesn’t recognise prior service from other Australian higher education institutions, staff are entitled to generous long service leave provisions after 7 years of service. Extended study leave Academic Staff can apply for the opportunity to take an extended period of leave to undertake research and other scholarly work to develop in their current position and to enhance their career. University libraries Staff can access Library resources from our six libraries located across the Fremantle, Broome and Sydney Campuses to assist you in your academic role or studies. Community and belonging Morning teas and social clubs Regular morning teas are hosted on each campus, along with other social gatherings held throughout the year as an opportunity to get to know each other and build community. Mass Daily mass services are offered on each campus for staff, students and members of the public to attend. Health and Wellbeing Discounted Bupa Health Fund membership Staff can access 6% discount on Bupa private health insurance as part of our Bupa corporate health plan. Find out more about joining BUPA or 6 weeks free in 2023 . Free flu vaccinations Staff can obtain free annual flu vaccinations on campus or obtain a redeemable pharmacy voucher for staff unable to attend on the day or for those based at rural sites Gym and fitness programs Staff on the Fremantle Campus can access the on-site gym and fitness programs available. Staff on the Sydney Campus can access discounted gym and pool memberships with: Fernwood Broadway Anytime Fitness Glebe Victoria Park Pool and other local swimming pools Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Staff can access free confidential counselling services through our EAP provider, Access Wellbeing Services, to assist staff with personal and work-related situations that are impacting on their wellbeing. Recognising staff achievements Promotion opportunities The University rewards and recognises outstanding achievement and sustained high performance of academic staff through the annual academic promotions process. Academic staff have the opportunity to apply for promotion to the next level of appointment, with assessment based on merit and academic achievement. Vice-Chancellor’s Awards The Vice Chancellor’s annual program of Promoting Excellence in Teaching, Learning & Supervision Awards promotes, recognises and rewards high quality teaching practices and learning outcomes of individuals, teams and Schools. Locations Online Fremantle Broome Sydney Clinical Schools Quicklinks Donations Alumni Library Faculties and schools Apply direct Emergency Contact us Visit us Uni store Jobs at UNDA Feedback News Events Sydney © 2026 The University of Notre Dame Australia CRICOS Provider Code: 01032F : TEQSA PRV12170 : RTO Code 0064 Privacy Terms of Use"
