me Fremantle Sydney Our community impact Jobs at UNDA Employment opportunities Staff benefits Contact us Make an enquiry Submit Apply now Study with us Main menu Study with us Explore our programs Study with us Explore our programs Undergraduate Postgraduate Graduate research Vocational Education and Training (VET) Microcredential Online programs Guides Why UNDA? Study with us Why UNDA? Meet our students Our Core Curriculum Applications and admissions Study with us Applications and admissions How to apply Admission requirements Admission pathways Recognition of prior learning Fees, costs and scholarships Study with us Fees, costs and scholarships Tuition fees Other costs Financial assistance Scholarships International students Study with us International students Full degree students Semester abroad at UNDA Moving to Australia Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students Study with us Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students Recognised events Cultural protocols Students Main menu Students Your enrolment Students Your enrolment Calendars and timetables Student Centre Enrolling in courses Enrolment changes Student forms Student policies Student ID and concession cards Exams, results and graduation Fees and payments Glossary of terms Getting started Students Getting started Orientation week Student life Students Student life Accommodation Student Associations Student clubs and societies Sports and recreation Volunteering and mentoring Chaplaincy Opportunities and experiences Students Opportunities and experiences Job opportunities and career events Global experiences Study abroad and exchange programs Short-term travel and study tours Study retreats In Altum Support Students Support ND Support Hubs Access and inclusion Study support IT support Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander support HDR student support International student support Regional and rural student support Career planning and resources Emergency contacts Health, safety and wellbeing Raise a concern or appeal Our Research Main menu Our Research Our focus Our Research Our focus Good lives Exceptional care Strong communities Institutes and initiatives Our Research Institutes and initiatives Institute for Ethics & Society Institute for Health Research Nulungu Research Institute Centre for the History of Philosophy Churack Chair of Chronic Pain Education and Research Global Catholic Studies Global Centre for Catholic Leaders Centre for Technology and Human Futures Integrity and ethics Our Research Integrity and ethics Research integrity Human Research Ethics Research Data Management Engage Main menu Engage Visit us Engage Visit us Sydney Open Day Alumni Engage Alumni Alumni news Alumni perks Alumni volunteering Honorary doctorates Stay connected Donations Engage Donations Greatest Need Student Grants Opportunity and Merit Scholarships Research Fund Gifts in Wills Capital Gifts School of Medicine Prizes Our donors Contact us Industry and business partnerships Career advisors and teachers Venue hire Events News About us Main menu About us Introducing UNDA Our Strategy About us Our Strategy Antisemitism Student Equity and Diversity Strategy Vision and objects About us Vision and objects Our traditions Governance and leadership About us Governance and leadership Our leadership Structure Compliance Act, statutes and regulations Policies, procedures and guidelines Annual Performance Our national faculties and schools About us Our national faculties and schools School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Health Sciences School of Law and Business School of Medicine School of Nursing & Midwifery School of Philosophy & Theology Pathways Our campuses and facilities About us Our campuses and facilities Broome Fremantle Sydney Our community impact Jobs at UNDA About us Jobs at UNDA Employment opportunities Staff benefits Contact us Apply Now Make an enquiry Library Student portal Staff Contact us Join the conversation, connect today. Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Twitter YouTube Home Jobs at UNDA Employment opportunities EOI - Academic Sessional (Foundation Years Group Tutor), School of Medicine Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram EOI - Academic Sessional (Foundation Years Group Tutor), School of Medicine APPLY How to Apply Position Description Need help? Ask Notre Dame For further information or enquiries, please contact People and Culture: jobs@nd.edu.au Employment Type Sessional Category Casual/ Sessional Location Sydney Department School of Medicine Share LinkedIn Facebook X Email EOI - Academic Sessional (Foundation Years Group Tutor), School of Medicine EOI – Academic Sessional ( Foundation Years Group Tutor ) S chool of Medicine Based on our Sydney Campus Friendly and collaborative work environment Rewarding opportunity offering career development About the university We believe in the power of education to transform lives, strengthen communities and help people become the best version of themselves. The University of Notre Dame Australia is a modern, national Catholic university that serves more than 12,000 students across its campuses in Fremantle, Broome and Sydney. With a community of over 1,000 academic and professional staff, Notre Dame is recognised for its personalised learning environment, strong graduate outcomes and holistic educational philosophy rooted in critical thinking, ethics and the Catholic intellectual tradition. About the role The National School of Medicine seeks to appoint Lecturers and Senior Lecturers in medicine to undertake the role of Group Tutors in the Foundation Years of the Doctor of Medicine program based at the Darlinghurst Site of the National School of Medicine, Sydney. These include Problem-Based Learning (PBL) Tutoring, Communication and Clinical Skills sessions, Clinical Debriefing sessions and other learning opportunities. Key Responsibilities Facilitate the following sessions in each week of the academic year with the allocated group of students: - problem based learning tutorials - clinical debriefing tutorial - clinical and communication skills training sessions; Participate in assessment and evaluation activities including marking and providing feedback in collaboration with the Assessments team. Attend meetings and professional development sessions as required by the Head of Foundation Years and the School. Participate in performance development activities as required by the school. Consult with students in relation to readings, weekly topics and assessment. Provide a high level of pastoral care to students Qualifications, skills & experience Possession of a Medical qualification registrable with AHPRA and a Fellowship of a relevant professional body or a PhD in a relevant discipline. Experience in teaching at master's level or higher or in medical, health or professional practice-based education settings. High level of interest in medical education and experience in teaching in small group tutorials. Keen interest in maintaining currency in scholarship and professional practice. Ability to, or a willingness to learn how to incorporate technology (e.g. Blackboard, Zoom, email, internet) into teaching and learning. Ability to deliver quality learning and teaching practices in multiple modes including online delivery. Ability to assess priority of tasks, manage workload and meet deadlines, in a busy education environment. Evidence of a high level of pastoral care to students. Benefits Fitness Passport on offer . Generous training and development opportunities. Friendly and collaborative working environment. How to apply If this sounds like you, please email a cover letter and your CV. Please specify your area of interest and subject matter expertise, as well as your availability, in your cover letter. We are looking for Academic Sessionals on an ongoing basis. We will be in contact should a role become available. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia and will need to comply with mandatory check requirements. The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to increase the diversity of our workforce to better meet the different needs of the University and its stakeholders and to improve equal opportunity outcomes for our staff. Enquiries about the role: Please contact Sharon Abraham sharon.abraham@nd.edu.au Back to current openings Locations Online Fremantle Broome Sydney Clinical Schools Quicklinks Donations Alumni Library Faculties and schools Apply direct Emergency Contact us Visit us Uni store Jobs at UNDA Feedback News Events Sydney © 2026 The University of Notre Dame Australia CRICOS Provider Code: 01032F : TEQSA PRV12170 : RTO Code 0064 Privacy Terms of Use"
