 Twitter YouTube Home Jobs at UNDA Employment opportunities EOI - Digital Learning and Design Intern Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram EOI - Digital Learning and Design Intern APPLY How to Apply Position Description Need help? Ask Notre Dame For further information or enquiries, please contact People and Culture: jobs@nd.edu.au Employment Type General Casual Category EOI Location Australia Department Innovation & Design Share LinkedIn Facebook X Email EOI - Digital Learning and Design Intern EOI - D igital Learning and Design Inter ns, Innovation and Design Fremantle or Sydney campus Casual opportuni ties on offer - Open to Notre Dame current students only Casual opportunities on offer for enrolled students who have completed at least one semester or more of study at The University of Notre Dame Australia . Join the University supporting its students and staff to achieve their career goals ( L evel 3 ) WA/NSW payrate + 14 .5 % superannuation About the university The University of Notre Dame Australia is a private Catholic University with over 1,000 permanent staff providing an exceptional educational experience to over 12,000 students across our Fremantle, Broome, and Sydney campuses, as well as clinical schools in Victoria an d New South Wales. About the office/school The Innovation & Design Office is responsible for the transformation of learning and teaching at the University through learning innovations, with an emphasis on expert pedagogy, instructional design, quality and digital technologies to enhance the student learning journey and meet the University’s Objects and strategic direction as a Catholic university. About the role The position contributes to implementing and sustaining high-quality online, blended/hybrid and face-to-face practice across the University and participates in a team approach to meet the University’s Objects and strategic direction as a Catholic university. This position is open to current enrolled student students who have completed at least one semester or more of study at The University of Notre Dame Australia. Students must have full Australian work rights. We encourage all current eligible students to apply. Key Responsibilities Create eye-catching graphics and simple videos to make learning more engaging. Support the look and feel of online content across the university’s LMS. Collaborate with staff from different teams on real learning design projects. Contribute ideas in meetings and stay updated on new learning tools. Grow your skills through hands-on experience and training opportunities. Assist with other tasks as needed by your mentor or team. Represent the university professionally by following policies and showing initiative. Qualifications, skills & experience Essential Completed at least 1 semester or more of study at The University of Notre Dame Australia, with at least 1 semester of study remaining. Ability to work approximately 5 -10 hours per week. Proficient in Microsoft Office, with basic skills in graphic design or video editing (Canva/Adobe Creative Cloud). Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to collaborate, seek guidance, and contribute to team efforts. Basic knowledge of digital tools and a strong interest in exploring modern technologies for teaching and learning. Basic knowledge of digital design principles and curiosity about current learning technologies. Strong time management skills with the ability to plan and track projects to meet deadlines, and a willingness to learn project management tools. Ability to work independently or as part of a team, support others, and learn from more experienced colleagues. Capable of assessing tasks, prioritising, and receiving feedback to address challenges. Willingness to adapt to new tools, workflows, and projects as needed. Desirable Participated in or helped coordinate a work-related project — such as organising a small even or improving a process. Has supported tasks that required organising information and identifying trends . Benefits Gain valuable hands-on experience in learning design whil st working with modern educational technologies . Friendly and collaborative working environment. How to apply Please apply online with a resume and cover letter outlining your suitability for the role . Also quote student number and duration of semester remaining until you graduate. Applications reviewed and interviewed when work is available. For further information on how to apply, please visit: How to apply | Notre Dame Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to increase the diversity of our workforce to better meet the different needs of the University and its stakeholders and to improve equal opportunity outcomes for our staff. The University is committed to providing a safe, respectful and inclusive working and learning environment. The successful candidate will be required to complete a self-declaration regarding Gender-Based Violence (as required by the National Code) as part of the pre-employment process. For more information on this please refer to our website. Contact us Please direct general queries regarding this role to Michelle Katavatis, Head of Innovation and Design - michelle.katavatis@nd.edu.au Unsolicited contact from recruitment agencies will not be entertained. Back to current openings Locations Online Fremantle Broome Sydney Clinical Schools Quicklinks Donations Alumni Library Faculties and schools Apply direct Emergency Contact us Visit us Uni store Jobs at UNDA Feedback News Events Sydney © 2026 The University of Notre Dame Australia CRICOS Provider Code: 01032F : TEQSA PRV12170 : RTO Code 0064 Privacy Terms of Use"
