 Twitter YouTube Home Jobs at UNDA Employment opportunities Lecturer (Nursing), School of Nursing and Midwifery Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram Lecturer (Nursing), School of Nursing and Midwifery APPLY How to Apply Position Description Need help? Ask Notre Dame For further information or enquiries, please contact People and Culture: jobs@nd.edu.au Employment Type Full-Time Category Nursing & Midwifery Location Fremantle Department School of Nursing & Midwifery Share LinkedIn Facebook X Email Lecturer (Nursing), School of Nursing and Midwifery Lecturer (Nursing) , School of Nursing and Midwifery Fremantle Campus Full-time opportunity , Continuing contract Friendly and collaborative work environment Rewarding opportunity offering career development $ 112,361 pa ( L evel B ) + 14 .5 % super *1st July EA increase to $116,294 p ro rata + 15% super About the university We believe in the power of education to transform lives, strengthen communities and help people become the best version of themselves. The University of Notre Dame Australia is a modern, national Catholic university that serves more than 12,000 students across its campuses in Fremantle, Broome and Sydney. With a community of over 1,000 academic and professional staff, Notre Dame is recognised for its personalised learning environment, strong graduate outcomes and holistic educational philosophy rooted in critical thinking, ethics and the Catholic intellectual tradition . About the school The School of Nursing and Midwifery is the University’s largest School and one of Australia’s premier providers of nursing and midwifery education. About the role This is a key position within the School of Nursing and Midwifery , responsible for teaching and coordinating nursing courses in undergraduate and postgraduate programs. The role also supports high-quality teaching informed by research and incorporates innovative online learning activities and assessments to ensure a high level of student satisfaction and effective pastoral care. Key Responsibilities Responsible for the preparation and delivery of substantial components of courses. Prepare and deliver curriculum components aligned with the staff member’s disciplinary and professional background. Provide leadership to other staff within the teaching team Undertake a range of activities to ensure the ongoing improvement of teaching practice. Attend School meetings as required and participate in School and University-wide committees and activities. Contribute to the scholarship of teaching and learning and/or professional practice within the discipline. Demonstrate a commitment to seeking and responding to feedback (from students, peers, and supervisors) to enhance teaching practice . Qualifications, skills & experience Hold a Bachelor of Nursing degree or equivalent, and a minimum postgraduate certificate qualification in a relevant discipline. Current registration as a nurse with AHPRA. At least three years of clinical nursing experience. Demonstrated ability to develop teaching resources and deliver courses in a variety of formats, including the effective use of online learning management systems within a tertiary environment. Excellent communication, time management, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively within a team Experience in teaching within a tertiary environment . Benefits Fast paced environment with opportunity for professional growth Generous training and development opportunities Friendly and collaborative working environment How to apply Please apply online with a resume and cover letter outlining your suitability for the role. Applications closing date: 8 September 2026 For further information on how to apply, please visit: How to apply | Notre Dame Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. The University is committed to providing a safe, respectful and inclusive working and learning environment. The successful candidate will be required to complete a self-declaration regarding Gender-Based Violence (as required by the National Code) as part of the pre-employment process. For more information on this please refer to our website. The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to increase the diversity of our workforce to better meet the different needs of the University and its stakeholders and to improve equal opportunity outcomes for our staff. Contact us Please direct your queries regarding this role to Melissa Schmidt (Talent Acquisition Partner) at melissa.schmidt@nd.edu.au Unsolicited contact from recruitment agencies will not be entertained. Back to current openings Locations Online Fremantle Broome Sydney Clinical Schools Quicklinks Donations Alumni Library Faculties and schools Apply direct Emergency Contact us Visit us Uni store Jobs at UNDA Feedback News Events Sydney © 2026 The University of Notre Dame Australia CRICOS Provider Code: 01032F : TEQSA PRV12170 : RTO Code 0064 Privacy Terms of Use"
