ern or appeal Our Research Main menu Our Research Our focus Our Research Our focus Good lives Exceptional care Strong communities Institutes and initiatives Our Research Institutes and initiatives Institute for Ethics & Society Institute for Health Research Nulungu Research Institute Centre for the History of Philosophy Churack Chair of Chronic Pain Education and Research Global Catholic Studies Global Centre for Catholic Leaders Centre for Technology and Human Futures Integrity and ethics Our Research Integrity and ethics Research integrity Human Research Ethics Research Data Management Engage Main menu Engage Visit us Engage Visit us Sydney Open Day Alumni Engage Alumni Alumni news Alumni perks Alumni volunteering Honorary doctorates Stay connected Donations Engage Donations Greatest Need Student Grants Opportunity and Merit Scholarships Research Fund Gifts in Wills Capital Gifts School of Medicine Prizes Our donors Contact us Industry and business partnerships Career advisors and teachers Venue hire Events News About us Main menu About us Introducing UNDA Our Strategy About us Our Strategy Antisemitism Student Equity and Diversity Strategy Vision and objects About us Vision and objects Our traditions Governance and leadership About us Governance and leadership Our leadership Structure Compliance Act, statutes and regulations Policies, procedures and guidelines Annual Performance Our national faculties and schools About us Our national faculties and schools School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Health Sciences School of Law and Business School of Medicine School of Nursing & Midwifery School of Philosophy & Theology Pathways Our campuses and facilities About us Our campuses and facilities Broome Fremantle Sydney Our community impact Jobs at UNDA About us Jobs at UNDA Employment opportunities Staff benefits Contact us Apply Now Make an enquiry Library Student portal Staff Contact us Join the conversation, connect today. Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Twitter YouTube Home Jobs at UNDA Employment opportunities Admissions Coordinator, Admissions Office Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram Admissions Coordinator, Admissions Office APPLY How to Apply Position Description Need help? Ask Notre Dame For further information or enquiries, please contact People and Culture: jobs@nd.edu.au Employment Type Full-Time Category Administrative Location Sydney Department Admissions Share LinkedIn Facebook X Email Admissions Coordinator, Admissions Office Admissions Coordinator Sydney campus Full- time opportunity, Continuin g contract Coordinate admissions activity that supports a smooth and positive applicant experience. J oin the university that takes a personalised approach to education $ 106,302 pa (level 6 ) + 1 5 % superannuation About the university We believe in the power of education to transform lives, strengthen communities and help people become the best version of themselves. The University of Notre Dame Australia is a modern, national Catholic university that serves more than 12,000 students across its campuses in Fremantle, Broome and Sydney. With a community of over 1,000 academic and professional staff, Notre Dame is recognised for its personalised learning environment, strong graduate outcomes and holistic educational philosophy rooted in critical thinking, ethics and the Catholic intellectual tradition. About the office The Admissions Office manages domestic applications to study at the University, including direct applications and applications through tertiary admission centres. The team works closely with Registry, Faculties and other University areas to assess applications, support enrolments and provide a smooth experience for applicants and internal stakeholders A bout the role The Admissions Coordinator helps manage the day-to-day admissions process for domestic students. The role works closely with Senior Admission Officers, Faculties, Schools and other teams to plan intake activities, manage key deadlines and offer rounds, monitor application progress, support readmissions and help resolve workflow issues. The role also supports staff training, maintains process documents and helps improve admissions processes to provide a positive applicant experience and supports the University’s enrolment goals. The position reports to the National Manager, Admissions. Key Responsibilities Coordinate domestic admissions activity across intake cycles, including key dates, offer rounds and application progress. Support consistent national admissions processes and help resolve workflow issues. Monitor application pipelines, identify delays and support timely follow-up. Coordinate offer release and ensure applicant communications are accurate and timely. Work with Faculties, Schools, Registry, Marketing and other teams to support admissions activity. Maintain accurate admissions information, process documents and system data. Support team training, compliance requirements and continuous process improvement. Qualifications, skills & experience Relevant degree or equivalent experience and training. Experience in domestic admissions, including application assessment, offers, deadlines and applicant communications. Strong planning, coordination and time management skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities. Ability to support team workflow, solve problems and identify risks or process issues. Strong communication and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to work with internal and external partners. Good systems skills, including Microsoft Office, student management systems, admissions platforms and databases. High attention to detail, with the ability to interpret policies, procedures and admissions requirements accurately. Commitment to compliance, confidentiality, data quality and continuous improvement . Benefits Ongoing training and development opportunities to help you grow and succeed in your career. A positive, supportive, and collaborative team environment. Discounted study at the University. How to apply Please apply online with a resume and cover letter outlining your suitability for the role. Applications closing date: 11 September 2026 For further information on how to apply, please visit: How to apply | Notre Dame Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to increase the diversity of our workforce to better meet the different needs of the University and its stakeholders and to improve equal opportunity outcomes for our staff. The University is committed to providing a safe, respectful and inclusive working and learning environment. The successful candidate will be required to complete a self-declaration regarding Gender-Based Violence (as required by the National Code) as part of the pre-employment process. For more information on this please refer to our website. Contact us Please direct your queries regarding this role to Marcia Rodrigues , Marcia.Rodrigues@nd.edu.au Unsolicited contact from recruitment agencies will not be entertained. Back to current openings Locations Online Fremantle Broome Sydney Clinical Schools Quicklinks Donations Alumni Library Faculties and schools Apply direct Emergency Contact us Visit us Uni store Jobs at UNDA Feedback News Events Sydney © 2026 The University of Notre Dame Australia CRICOS Provider Code: 01032F : TEQSA PRV12170 : RTO Code 0064 Privacy Terms of Use"
