 Twitter YouTube Home Jobs at UNDA Employment opportunities National Senior Student Support Officer - VET Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram National Senior Student Support Officer - VET APPLY How to Apply Position Description Need help? Ask Notre Dame For further information or enquiries, please contact People and Culture: jobs@nd.edu.au Employment Type Full-Time Category Administrative Location Fremantle Department Vocational Education & Training Share LinkedIn Facebook X Email National Senior Student Support Officer - VET National Senior Student Support Officer , V ET Fremantle Campus Full-time opportunity, Fixed term c ontract ending August 2027 Support VET administration and student services. Competitive Salary + 15% superannuation . About the university We believe in the power of education to transform lives, strengthen communities and help people become the best version of themselves. The University of Notre Dame Australia is a modern, national Catholic u niversity that serves more than 12,000 students across its campuses in Fremantle, Broome and Sydney. With a community of over 1,000 academic and professional staff, Notre Dame is recognised for its personalised learning environment, strong graduate outcomes and holistic educational philosophy rooted in critical thinking, ethics and the Catholic intellectual tradition . About the office Vocational Education and Training (VET) at Notre Dame provides students with the skills they need to thrive in the education and health industries. We provide career preparation and formal qualifications to specialise in a certain area of work, to make a career change or as a pathway into higher education. Our programs are flexible and structured so students can learn online, on-campus a n d in the field. About the role The National Senior Student Support Officer coordinates administrative and student support activities across all VET programs, including program delivery, compliance, reporting and stakeholder engagement. Working closely with senior leaders, the position supports continuous improvement initiatives to enhance processes, service delivery and student outcomes. The position reports to the Operations Manager, Vocational Education and Training (VET). Key Responsibilities Coordinate VET administration while supporting team performance and positive student outcomes. Oversee records, compliance, reporting, events, projects and budgets. Resolve complex student and administrative matters. Drive process improvements to enhance service delivery and student outcomes. Build strong relationships with students, staff and external stakeholders. Qualifications, skills & experience Relevant degree with demonstrated experience, or an equivalent combination of education, training and professional experience. Proven experience leading administrative support and coordination, preferably within a VET, RTO or education environment. Experience in financial administration, procurement and project coordination. Ability to provide advice and support to senior leaders on administration, compliance, policy and process improvement. Strong administrative, project and process management skills, with excellent attention to detail and the ability to manage competing priorities. Strong analytical, problem-solving and initiative-taking skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage and influence staff, students and external stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to improve administrative systems, processes and service delivery. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, with experience using LMS and CRM systems. Ability to lead, motivate and develop a team through guidance, mentoring and professional support. Knowledge of ASQA compliance, government-funded programs and VET operational requirements is highly desirable. Benefits Generous training and development opportunities. Friendly and collaborative working environment. Discounted study at the University. How to apply Please apply online with a resume and cover letter outlining your suitability for the role. Applications closing date: 14 September 2026 For further information on how to apply, please visit: How to apply | Notre Dame Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. The University is committed to providing a safe, respectful and inclusive working and learning environment. The successful candidate will be required to complete a self-declaration regarding Gender-Based Violence (as required by the National Code) as part of the pre-employment process. For more information on this please refer to our website. The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to increase the diversity of our workforce to better meet the different needs of the University and its stakeholders and to improve equal opportunity outcomes for our staff. Contact us Please direct your queries regarding this role to Marcia Rodrigues , Marcia.Rodrigues@nd.edu.au Unsolicited contact from recruitment agencies will not be entertained. Back to current openings Locations Online Fremantle Broome Sydney Clinical Schools Quicklinks Donations Alumni Library Faculties and schools Apply direct Emergency Contact us Visit us Uni store Jobs at UNDA Feedback News Events Sydney © 2026 The University of Notre Dame Australia CRICOS Provider Code: 01032F : TEQSA PRV12170 : RTO Code 0064 Privacy Terms of Use"
